{"type":"after","callId":"jgqi@2080","endTime":321136.034,"result":{"value":"All projects\nWEB EXPERIENCE / 10\nMercury Mailroom.\n\nA workplace mailroom system for mail-piece management, delivery tracking, and organization settings.\n\nPROJECT TYPE\nWeb & web apps\nFOCUS\nWorkplace operations\nORIGINAL PROJECT ARTWORK\nOverview\nKey features\nDesign\nScreenshots\nDevice views\n01\nPROJECT OVERVIEW\nGive every mail piece a place.\n\nClarigo’s Mercury Mailroom source describes managing mail pieces and tracking their delivery inside a company workspace. It identifies employee, department, location, sender, and address records, together with access permissions tied to user privileges. The supplied artwork shows a settings-focused desktop interface and an account-entry screen.\n\n02\nKEY FEATURES\nA closer look at\nthe experience.\n\nThe flows and interface elements visible in Mercury Mailroom's original project material.\n\n01\nMail-piece tracking\n\nThe published overview identifies mail-piece management and delivery tracking.\n\n02\nOrganization records\n\nEmployee and department information form part of the described workspace.\n\n03\nLocation information\n\nMail stops, workstations, and addresses support internal routing.\n\n04\nAccess permissions\n\nThe source describes permissions based on user type or privileges.\n\n03\nDESIGN DIRECTION\nIts own identity.\nIn every detail.\nWorkplace operations\n\nBlue navigation and a persistent left rail frame a dense settings workspace. Clearly divided panels allow configuration lists and detailed values to appear together, while a lighter sign-in screen preserves the same restrained visual identity.\n\nDesign observations from the supplied project artwork.\n04\nUI SCREENSHOTS & ARTWORK\nInside Mercury Mailroom.\n\nExplore the original design compositions. Select any image for a closer look.\n\nDESIGN COMPOSITION\n01\n05\nRESPONSIVE DESIGN PRESENTATION\nA view across\nthe original devices.\n\nMercury Mailroom's original portfolio composition presents the website on laptop and tablet devices. The artwork below preserves those supplied layouts together, with their original proportions.\n\nThese are source mockups of the project, rather than a new rendering of its live website.\n\nMercury Mailroom / Original device composition\nSOURCE MATERIAL\n\nProject descriptions are based on the published artwork and available overview. Interface observations do not imply verified implementation details or measured business results.\n\nOriginal project page\nNEXT WEB PROJECT\nUmeed\nKEEP EXPLORING\nMore perspectives.\nView all work\nMATRIMONY & DISCOVERY\nUmeed\nEDUCATION & SERVICES\nAlum-connect\nEXERCISE & WELLBEING\nKegelklock\nHAVE A PROJECT IN MIND?\nLet's make your\nnext idea real.\nBook a free consultation"}}
